{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc | sed -n '625,735p'; cat collab/1790463610624-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice0-gate.gpt-6-sol.findings.md; cat collab/1790463620000-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice0-fixes.glm-flash.report.md\"","aggregated_output":"   625\t   mints nothing. Recovering a gap is the caller's decision, made on the\n   626\t   recovery cursor a gap report carries; nothing here resynchronizes\n   627\t   anything on its own.\"\n   628\t  [state index cursor]\n   629\t  (assoc-in state [:members index :cursor] cursor))\n   630\t\n   631\t\n   632\t(defn observe-step!\n   633\t  \"Walk the intake pool once from (:next state) and process at most one\n   634\t   payload, through dao.stream.observe/step with materialize! as the\n   635\t   effect. Returns {:state next-state :signal s ...} where the signal is\n   636\t   drawn from the same eight outcomes dao.stream declares for next:\n   637\t\n   638\t     {:signal :dao.stream/ok, :address a}\n   639\t       a payload was materialized; the member advanced to the successor\n   640\t       cursor its stream returned, and yields its turn;\n   641\t     {:signal :dao.stream/blocked}\n   642\t       the pool is empty, or every non-ended member answered blocked;\n   643\t     {:signal :dao.stream/end}\n   644\t       every member has ended;\n   645\t     {:signal :dao.stream/gap, :member i, :cursor recovery}\n   646\t       member i's position was evicted;\n   647\t     {:signal k, :member i, :result read}\n   648\t       k is :dao.stream/cursor-mismatch, :dao.stream/invalid-cursor,\n   649\t       :dao.stream/transport-error, or :dao.stream/refused -- or, for a\n   650\t       well-formed outcome outside this contract version, that outcome\n   651\t       itself, which the step classifies as refused.\n   652\t\n   653\t   gap and defect reports leave the member's cursor unchanged and move\n   654\t   :next past the member, so the same condition is reported again on that\n   655\t   member's next turn; nothing is auto-resynchronized. A defect carries the\n   656\t   raw read under :result exactly as the step classified it -- a transport\n   657\t   that answered with something that is not a well-formed outcome map is\n   658\t   reported with its answer retained, never folded into a meaning nobody\n   659\t   chose. A refused read reports the same way under its own outcome: a\n   660\t   policy declined the member's read, nothing was observed, and the member\n   661\t   keeps its cursor -- and an unrecognized outcome reports this way too,\n   662\t   a newer contract being a refusal, not a defect. Blocked and\n   663\t   ended members never prevent later members from being checked, and a\n   664\t   member that yielded a payload loses its turn, so a continuously ready\n   665\t   member cannot starve another.\n   666\t\n   667\t   The effect is materialize!, which answers ok or throws: :failed is\n   668\t   unreachable, and a throwing effect propagates before any cursor moves,\n   669\t   so the caller's state is untouched and the same payload is reprocessed\n   670\t   from the same cursor once the backend succeeds.\"\n   671\t  [handle state]\n   672\t  (let [n (count (:members state))]\n   673\t    (if (zero? n)\n   674\t      {:state state, :signal :dao.stream/blocked}\n   675\t      (let [effect (fn [payload]\n   676\t                     {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   677\t                      :address (materialize! handle payload)})]\n   678\t        (loop [i (:next state)\n   679\t               scanned 0\n   680\t               state' state]\n   681\t          (if (>= scanned n)\n   682\t            {:state state'\n   683\t             :signal (if (every? #(= :dao.stream/end (:status %))\n   684\t                                 (:members state'))\n   685\t                       :dao.stream/end\n   686\t                       :dao.stream/blocked)}\n   687\t            (let [member (nth (:members state') i)\n   688\t                  r (observe/step (:stream member) (:cursor member) effect)]\n   689\t              (case (:status r)\n   690\t                :advance\n   691\t                {:state (-> state'\n   692\t                            (assoc-in [:members i :cursor] (:cursor r))\n   693\t                            (assoc-in [:members i :status] :dao.stream/ok)\n   694\t                            (assoc :next (mod (inc i) n)))\n   695\t                 :signal :dao.stream/ok\n   696\t                 :address (get-in r [:effect :address])}\n   697\t                :retry\n   698\t                (recur (mod (inc i) n)\n   699\t                       (inc scanned)\n   700\t                       (assoc-in state' [:members i :status]\n   701\t                                 :dao.stream/blocked))\n   702\t                :ended\n   703\t                (recur (mod (inc i) n)\n   704\t                       (inc scanned)\n   705\t                       (assoc-in state' [:members i :status] :dao.stream/end))\n   706\t                :gap\n   707\t                {:state (-> state'\n   708\t                            (assoc-in [:members i :status] :dao.stream/gap)\n   709\t                            (assoc :next (mod (inc i) n)))\n   710\t                 :signal :dao.stream/gap\n   711\t                 :member i\n   712\t                 :cursor (:recovery r)}\n   713\t                :refused\n   714\t                {:state (-> state'\n   715\t                            (assoc-in [:members i :status] (:outcome r))\n   716\t                            (assoc :next (mod (inc i) n)))\n   717\t                 :signal (:outcome r)\n   718\t                 :member i\n   719\t                 :result (:read r)}\n   720\t                :defect\n   721\t                {:state (-> state'\n   722\t                            (assoc-in [:members i :status] (:outcome r))\n   723\t                            (assoc :next (mod (inc i) n)))\n   724\t                 :signal (:outcome r)\n   725\t                 :member i\n   726\t                 :result (:read r)}\n   727\t                :failed\n   728\t                (throw (ex-info\n   729\t                         \"unreachable: the DaoJing effect answers ok or throws\"\n   730\t                         {:result r, :member i}))))))))))\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-09-26 23:01:14 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-27 06:01:14 Indochina Time\n\nP1 | [src/cljc/dao/stream/observe.cljc:51](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/observe.cljc:51) | An unrecognized outcome is converted to `transport-error`, then classified as a defect or failed effect. This contradicts the [contract’s unrecognized-outcome rule](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:113). | Preserve a well-formed unrecognized outcome and classify it as refused; retain malformed-answer handling separately.\n\nP1 | [src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1373](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1373) | A parked `:next` or `:put` waking with an unrecognized outcome reaches `throw-terminal-resume!`, while the [immediate path returns a shaped refusal](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:390). The blocked-must-not-change law therefore fails. | Shape unrecognized wake outcomes as refusals and allow them through resume; keep declared error outcomes terminal.\n\nThe reported JVM, Node, and Dart suites passed; I did not rerun them.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\nSign-off: DENIED## P1-1 — observe.cljc: unrecognized outcome became transport-error/defect instead of refused\n\n- `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/observe.cljc:44-63` — `valid-or-transport-error` now classifies via `stream/validate-outcome`: a well-formed outcome map whose keyword lies outside the operation's declared set (`:unauthorized-outcome`, i.e. a newer contract per `docs/design/dao.stream.md:113`) is preserved exactly as it arrived; only truly malformed answers (non-map, missing/unqualified keyword, declared outcome missing required keys) still fold into `transport-error`.\n- `observe.cljc:150-159` — the read `case`'s default clause now classifies a preserved unrecognized outcome as `:refused` (cursor unchanged, outcome preserved, raw read retained); `cursor-mismatch`/`invalid-cursor`/`transport-error` keep their explicit `:defect` clause, so malformed stays defect.\n- Effect side: an unrecognized write outcome falls into the existing default `:failed` branch (the established refused mapping), with `:outcome` preserved and the raw answer under `:effect`.\n- Docstring: intro + status table rewritten (`observe.cljc:67-95`) to add unrecognized to `:refused` (reads) and `:failed` (effects) and keep malformed under `:defect`/`transport-error`.\n\n## P1-2 — engine.cljc:1373 (now 1396): parked :next/:put waking unrecognized threw while the immediate path refused\n\n- `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:311-344` — new private data + predicate: `wake-error-outcomes` (the declared defects per reason: `cursor-mismatch`/`invalid-cursor`/`transport-error` for `:next`; `closed`/`invalid-value`/`transport-error` for `:put`), `wake-value-statuses` (`nil`/`:ok`/`:end`/`:gap` for a reader, `nil`/`:ok` for a writer), and `wake-refusal?` (refused or any status outside those two sets).\n- `engine.cljc:346-373` — `make-woken-run-queue-entries` now shapes every `wake-refusal?` status into the same shaped refusal the immediate `handle-put`/`handle-next` return (`{:status :refused, :outcome <status>, :stream-id id}` plus `:cursor-id` for readers).\n- `engine.cljc:1396-1414` — `terminal-resume-outcome` now raises only waitset diagnostics, `:link-refused`, and the per-reason declared error outcomes; unrecognized statuses pass through to the restore as data. Declared error outcomes stay terminal.\n\n## Tests added\n\n- `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/dao/stream/observe_test.cljc:165` `an-unrecognized-read-is-refused-with-its-own-outcome` (well-formed unknown read outcomes classify `:refused`, preserved, cursor kept); `:192` `an-unrecognized-effect-answer-fails-as-refused-does` (unknown/end-on-append classify `:failed`, preserved). Malformed-answer tests trimmed of the now-refused/mis-set answers.\n- `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/engine_test.cljc:503` `a-woken-unrecognized-entry-resumes-as-data-test` — four blocks: parked reader waking `:dao.stream/quantum-flux` resumes the exact shaped refusal as data; parked writer waking unrecognized refuses in `handle-put`'s shape (no cursor-id/update); declared read and write defects still raise on resume with the immediate path's ex-data.\n\nAlso `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:647-663` — docstring-only correction (no behavior change): `observe-step!`'s signal list now notes that a well-formed outcome outside the contract reports under its own keyword via the refused path.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Static: `cljstyle check` clean on all five files (one indentation nit found and fixed); clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings (only pre-existing info at `engine.cljc:276`, verified present at HEAD); added lines pure ASCII and <= 80 columns; no diagnostics left; only the five permitted files modified; no git state operations.\n- Lanes run sequentially, solo:\n  - JVM (`clojure -M:test`): Ran 2217 tests containing 182889 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors. (baseline 2,214/182,863/0)\n  - Node (shadow-cljs `slice-peer test` compile + `node target/node-tests.js`): Ran 2129 tests containing 49555 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors. (baseline 2,126/49,532/0)\n  - Dart (`clojure -M:cljd test` after both peer exe builds): +2091: All tests passed! (baseline 2,088)\n\nStatus: COMPLETE","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
